          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %strong identity function
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_S\colon S \to S
            that maps any element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to itself:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi λ
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi x
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_S = (x \mapsto x) = \lambda x.\; x ;
          %p or equivalently,
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_S(x) = x .
          %p
            Thus, the identity function is the function for which every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
          %p
            The identity functions are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
            in the category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of sets.
          %p
            More generally, in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+set"} underlying set
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              In (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"}> dependent
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
